{"duration_api_ms":3629,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6859d5f9-3206-4a04-adc6-ce92d3baace7","total_cost_usd":0.0007264999999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1084,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":676,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":278},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1084,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1084,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1084},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1627,"outputTokens":694,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1084,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0007264999999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":278,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":1084,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Existing contract:** A change of control of the principal adviser is an \"assignment\" under Section 2(a)(4) of the Investment Company Act of 1940, and the existing advisory contract terminates automatically at closing (Section 15(a)(4)).\n\n**New contract approvals:**\n- **Board:** The board, including a majority of independent trustees voting in person at a meeting called for that purpose, must approve the new contract (Section 15(c)).\n- **Shareholders:** A majority of the fund's outstanding voting securities must approve it (Section 15(a)(2)).\n- **Interim contract:** Rule 15a-4 allows an interim contract for up to 150 days after termination, if the board approves it and the adviser's fees are held in escrow pending shareholder approval.\n- **Terms:** The contract must be in writing and terminable without penalty on 60 days' notice by the board or a majority of outstanding shares (Section 15(a)(3)).\n\n**Related consideration:** Section 15(f) provides a safe harbor for an adviser receiving payments tied to a change of control. For three years after closing, at least 75% of the board must not be \"interested persons\" of the adviser, and the fund must not bear an unfair burden.","ttft_ms":1971,"type":"result","duration_ms":3124,"uuid":"b252e595-362d-4736-b2e2-02e809abeb78","ttft_stream_ms":868,"time_to_request_ms":61,"first_content_frame_ms":868,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
